      "essence": "Organized responsibility in service of a shared aim gives The Army a path beyond force, passivity, or premature certainty.",
      "summary": "The Daoist lens attends to how force can accord with the configuration instead of contending with it. In The Army, the central situation is collective force requiring disciplined direction, and the commentarial evidence repeatedly emphasizes leader, right, and advancing. The main danger is power dispersing or becoming coercive, especially when partial conditions are mistaken for permission to press ahead. Its constructive capacity is organized responsibility in service of a shared aim, expressed through attention to sequence, relation, and the limits of the present position. Transformation comes through responsive timing: capacity remains available because it is neither suppressed nor spent against the grain.",
